## Building a Contact Book

A contact entry captures the three essentials: who they are, how to call them, and how to email them.

### The Contact Struct

```xiom
type Contact = {
  name: Str;
  phone: Str;
  email: Str;
}
```

### Creating Contacts

```xiom
let alice = Contact{ name: "Alice Chen"; phone: "555-0101"; email: "alice@email.com"; };
let bob = Contact{ name: "Bob Smith"; phone: "555-0202"; email: "bob@email.com"; };
let charlie = Contact{ name: "Charlie Park"; phone: "555-0303"; email: "charlie@email.com"; };
```

### Displaying a Contact

```xiom
fn Contact.display(self) -> Str {
  return name + " | " + phone + " | " + email;
}
```

### Searching by Name

A method that checks if a search term appears anywhere in the contact's name:

```xiom
fn Contact.matches(self, search: Str) -> Bool {
  return name == search;
}
```

For a simple exact match, compare names directly. For partial matching, check if the name contains the search text.

### Using the Contact Book

```xiom
alice.display();              // "Alice Chen | 555-0101 | alice@email.com"
alice.matches("Alice Chen");  // true
alice.matches("Bob");         // false
```

